        "text": "I'm planning out the markdown sample structure: headers at three levels, a nested bullet list three deep, a numbered list, a task list with mixed checked items, a 5-column table with header plus four rows, plus a markdown link and a bare URL.\n\nI'm constructing a 40-character hex hash for the inline code example, counting it out in groups of ten to make sure it lands exactly at 40 characters, then planning a blockquote, horizontal rule, and a TypeScript code block containing a single line around 90 characters—carefully drafting and recounting a function call example to hit that length.\n\nI'm also sketching a three-level nested list and a five-column table with four rows, and weighing whether to wrap the whole markdown sample in a fence so the raw syntax is visible rather than rendered, possibly using a four-backtick outer fence to accommodate the nested code block.\n\n",
